So like, what got you into it as a child?

00:08:11.370 --> 00:08:12.905
Like what did you, what did you catch?

00:08:12.905 --> 00:08:14.550
- I love storytelling.

00:08:14.550 --> 00:08:16.560
I think that's probably what
I am more than anything else.

00:08:16.560 --> 00:08:17.959
I love storytelling.

00:08:17.959 --> 00:08:19.380
I loved writing.

00:08:19.380 --> 00:08:22.620
I loved, you know, character building,

00:08:22.620 --> 00:08:26.310
for a kid without, you
know, a Hollywood budget.

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:28.440
It was making your own TV show,

00:08:28.440 --> 00:08:30.270
making your own film series.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:33.005
So for me that was like, are
you, you know, you kidding me?

00:08:33.005 --> 00:08:36.570
And then I could, the kids would
play characters in my show,

00:08:36.570 --> 00:08:38.730
that I ran every day, or every week.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.470
- I think that's so cool.

00:08:40.470 --> 00:08:41.303
I love it.

00:08:41.303 --> 00:08:43.080
So wait, so have you ever
gotten in a physical fight?

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:45.180
It can be a subjective event, right?

00:08:45.180 --> 00:08:47.414
So have you ever gotten in a
physical fight at "D and D"?

00:08:47.414 --> 00:08:48.247
- No, at "D and D"?

00:08:49.620 --> 00:08:50.970
I mean, when I was a kid, people-

00:08:50.970 --> 00:08:53.423
- Wait, or maybe not in "D
and D", what's happening?

00:08:55.012 --> 00:08:56.085
- Well, clearly, yeah.

00:08:56.085 --> 00:08:57.199
I mean, I've thrown some-

00:08:57.199 --> 00:08:58.032
- Bubba comes out.

00:08:58.032 --> 00:09:00.210
- I was a bouncer and a
bodyguard in college, so-

00:09:00.210 --> 00:09:01.375
- You were?

00:09:01.375 --> 00:09:02.208
- Yeah, yeah.
- Oh wow.

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:04.143
- That's a whole other
story for another time.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:06.300
- For a nighttime show.

00:09:06.300 --> 00:09:07.650
- Maybe. Yeah, probably.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:09.090
Yes, exactly.

00:09:09.090 --> 00:09:11.250
But no, when I was a kid, you know,

00:09:11.250 --> 00:09:12.450
there was a stigma against it.

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:14.550
You know, the churches were burning books.

00:09:14.550 --> 00:09:17.550
They thought that Satan was
possessing their children

00:09:17.550 --> 00:09:18.780
through the game.

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.199
That's the reputation that it had.

00:09:20.199 --> 00:09:21.032
- I did not know that.

00:09:21.032 --> 00:09:22.530
- And so the churches were burning books,

00:09:22.530 --> 00:09:24.900
and then the sales quadrupled,

00:09:24.900 --> 00:09:27.050
because the kids whose
books were being burned,

00:09:27.050 --> 00:09:30.270
went and bought more,
and then hid them better.

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.873
- And once you make it a red button,

00:09:31.873 --> 00:09:33.363
you just wanna press it.

00:09:33.363 --> 00:09:34.680
- Soon as your parents were upset,-

00:09:34.680 --> 00:09:35.513
- What's in there?

00:09:35.513 --> 00:09:36.346
- I need that.

00:09:36.346 --> 00:09:39.060
And so as a kid there was
a lot of stigma against it.

00:09:39.060 --> 00:09:41.208
So there were kids that would say things,

00:09:41.208 --> 00:09:43.560
and you'd get into almost
fights with kids over it.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:46.638
Or I'd defend other nerdy kids,

00:09:46.638 --> 00:09:47.736
I was friends with.

00:09:47.736 --> 00:09:49.631
I was a captain of the
football team, so I was-

00:09:49.631 --> 00:09:52.650
- Playing "Dungeons and
Dragons", I love it.

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.060
- So not necessarily that,

00:09:54.060 --> 00:09:56.160
but sometimes there's
arguments that happen when

00:09:56.160 --> 00:09:57.090
you're playing at the table.

00:09:57.090 --> 00:09:59.910
People want, they want to
tell you how the rules work.

00:09:59.910 --> 00:10:02.820
And I'm like, I know the
guy who wrote that rule.

00:10:02.820 --> 00:10:04.710
I was just on the phone
with him, the other day

00:10:04.710 --> 00:10:07.590
talking about some project
we're doing together.

00:10:07.590 --> 00:10:10.740
So the rule is the way it
is, you need to listen to me.

00:10:10.740 --> 00:10:11.826
And that's it.

00:10:11.826 --> 00:10:13.350
- I love, you're a rule baller.

00:10:13.350 --> 00:10:14.220
I am too.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:15.630
Wait, did you ever, come
to the football team?

00:10:15.630 --> 00:10:17.790
Did you ever think about
actually doing like,

00:10:17.790 --> 00:10:18.886
professional sports?
- No.

00:10:18.886 --> 00:10:20.370
- 'Cause you're like a big dude.

00:10:20.370 --> 00:10:22.230
- Well, there was a lot of talk,

00:10:22.230 --> 00:10:25.475
and actually when my the
high school theater teacher

00:10:25.475 --> 00:10:27.780
came to me and said
would you please try out?

00:10:27.780 --> 00:10:29.580
'Cause I made my own movies.

00:10:29.580 --> 00:10:32.482
And that kind of led to the
people saying you should

00:10:32.482 --> 00:10:34.290
be an actor, you should try this.

00:10:34.290 --> 00:10:36.630
And so the, the high school
theater teacher said,

00:10:36.630 --> 00:10:38.700
would you please try out for "Oklahoma"?

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.980
And I said, what do I
have to sing and dance?

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:42.750
She said, just sing Happy Birthday.

00:10:42.750 --> 00:10:44.790
So, you know, to Cindy
Shriner, my teacher,

00:10:44.790 --> 00:10:46.650
and she's kind of responsible, you know,

00:10:46.650 --> 00:10:48.930
in large part for pushing me into it.

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:51.750
So I went to the tryout,
I sang Happy Birthday

00:10:51.750 --> 00:10:54.360
I did some kind of dance,
and then that was it.

00:10:54.360 --> 00:10:55.440
I forgot about it.

00:10:55.440 --> 00:10:58.350
A few months later, kids
in the hallway were saying,

00:10:58.350 --> 00:10:59.400
Congrats Joe.

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:00.630
And I'm like, for what?

00:11:00.630 --> 00:11:02.910
And they're like, oh, you got
a huge part in the musical.

00:11:02.910 --> 00:11:04.090
And I went, Oh no.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:04.923
You know, I went and looked at that.

00:11:04.923 --> 00:11:05.800
- And you have to memorize everything.

00:11:05.800 --> 00:11:07.920
- Well, that was easy.
- It was?

00:11:07.920 --> 00:11:09.270
Memorizing was never easy for me.

00:11:09.270 --> 00:11:10.103
I was in musical theater.

00:11:10.103 --> 00:11:11.098
It was the hardest thing for me.

00:11:11.098 --> 00:11:12.570
- Oh, I can read it like once or twice.

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:16.233
- I'm not like, I don't
retain anything really.

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:19.800
- Yeah. It's a hard life with that.

00:11:19.800 --> 00:11:20.633
Yeah. I don't retain.

00:11:20.633 --> 00:11:22.230
- You landed on your feet, however.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:23.880
- With a teleprompter, yeah.

00:11:23.880 --> 00:11:24.808
- You've done all right.

00:11:24.808 --> 00:11:28.290
But so I, but the real problem was

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:30.360
that I was the captain
of the volleyball team.

00:11:30.360 --> 00:11:32.280
And I had, I was a four year starter.

00:11:32.280 --> 00:11:34.986
I was a junior Olympian, I
mean the Junior Olympic team.

00:11:34.986 --> 00:11:37.950
And then I, the musicals in the spring.

00:11:37.950 --> 00:11:39.180
So-

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.160
- You're like Wolverine,
like Hugh Jackman.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:43.230
You're like Wolverine and "Music Man".

00:11:43.230 --> 00:11:44.100
This is like awesome.

00:11:44.100 --> 00:11:44.933
It's like-

00:11:44.933 --> 00:11:47.220
- So all the coaches were really mad.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:48.120
They thought, they told,

00:11:48.120 --> 00:11:50.760
they made a point to tell me
how stupid they thought I was,

00:11:50.760 --> 00:11:52.650
and what a huge mistake I was making.

00:11:52.650 --> 00:11:54.120
And that I was throwing away.

00:11:54.120 --> 00:11:57.047
- Neener coaches, neener, neener.

00:11:57.047 --> 00:11:59.200
It worked out.

00:11:59.200 --> 00:12:00.630
It is a hard choice though.

00:12:00.630 --> 00:12:01.530
I love sports too.

00:12:01.530 --> 00:12:03.389
It's a hard choice, sometimes.

00:12:03.389 --> 00:12:04.222
- Yeah. I was an art, but I mean I was,

00:12:04.222 --> 00:12:06.240
I was more of an artist
than anything else.

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:09.260
So for me to not choose
to do that would've been

00:12:09.260 --> 00:12:10.723
the biggest crime for me,

00:12:10.723 --> 00:12:12.935
I had to do something I was gonna love.

00:12:12.935 --> 00:12:14.583
- [Kelly] I love that.

